      "body": "## Motivation\r\n\r\nBucketed RL weight synchronization calls `update_weights_from_tensor()` once per bucket. Each call currently forces a full Python garbage collection before returning, adding repeated pauses to the synchronization path. A downstream Nsight Systems capture measured 16.49–17.16 seconds inside these GC ranges per engine across 32 buckets.\r\n\r\n## Modifications\r\n\r\nRemove `gc.collect()` from the ordinary, non-LoRA tensor update path. Automatic GC, `torch.cuda.empty_cache()`, weight loading, and cache invalidation remain unchanged.\r\n\r\nDisk and LoRA cleanup policies remain unchanged because this PR's measurements and validation cover only ordinary tensor updates.\r\n\r\n## Accuracy Tests\r\n\r\n- Existing CPU regression: `TestWeightsUpdaterFusedParams` — 2 passed.\r\n- CPU check with the actual `WeightsUpdater` and `FlattenedTensorBucket`: 32 consecutive updates produced correct values, preserved destination storage identities, and released source tensors after caller references were removed. Only CUDA cache cleanup was mocked.\r\n- A downstream eight-GPU run completed a full RL cycle, with all eight engines reporting the updated weight version and healthy status.\r\n- Applicable pre-commit checks passed for the changed file.\r\n\r\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\r\n\r\nMeasured in a downstream SGLang v0.5.21 integration with eight colocated training/inference GPUs, 512 MiB buckets, and 32 buckets per engine. Each timing run covered one RL cycle with profiling disabled.\r\n\r\n| Measurement | Before | After |\r\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\r\n| Weight bucket loop | 22.8 s | 2.7 s |\r\n| Transport/wait portion of that loop | 21.8 s | 2.0 s |\r\n| Complete RL cycle | 153.97 s | 130.50 s |\r\n| Sampled peak GPU memory per device | 53.93 GiB | 53.90 GiB |\r\n\r\nComplete RL cycle time decreased by 15.24%.\r\n\r\nBefore the change: repeated GC pauses during bucketed weight updates. The `engine.weight_bucket_gc` NVTX range was added for profiling and directly wraps `gc.collect()` inside update_weights_from_tensor(). Across 32 buckets, these GC ranges total 17.16 seconds for this engine.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"961\" height=\"474\" alt=\"Snipaste_2026-10-23_00-45-47\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2ec68814-9601-47bf-a189-faffe7af4f84\" />\r\n\r\n\r\nZooming into one bucket: `engine.receive_weight_bucket` takes 530.056 ms, of which 502.341 ms (94.8%) is spent inside `gc.collect()`. This cleanup runs after every bucket, adding repeated pauses to the weight synchronization path.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1150\" height=\"450\" alt=\"part\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c2a2835e-c833-43a2-9843-2ba2e617d522\" />\r\n\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [x] Applicable pre-commit checks passed for the changed file.\r\n- [x] CPU regression and repeated-update checks passed.\r\n- [x] Performance results documented.\r\n- [ ] Full-repository pre-commit completed; interrupted during isort.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\r\n---\r\n### CI States\r\n\r\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39803121964](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39803121964)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\r\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: **Blocked** -- `run-ci` is required first.<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\r\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39803121786](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39803121786)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\r\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
